@DDvO I don't know whether you saw the thread on openssl-security, but the issue here is not really the error code, but the fact that the behaviour in 3.0 is cert-order-dependent.  And the reason for that is that with 3.0 the certificate with the matching SKID is not found when earlier cert with the same CA subject DN appears first in CAfile.

The OP has three potential issuer certs for the EE cert in the CAfile, cer1 has a matching SKID, while cert2 and cert3 do not.  When the CAfile is reversed, cert3 is read first and its mismatching SKID causes the error to be a SKID mismatch, rather than a failure to find a parent issuer for cert1.

This is at least a behaviour change from 1.1, and could actually be a problem if cert1 were a valid trust-anchor, or had a parent TA in the CAfile.  As it is, all three ultimately fail.

@metsma, thanks for reporting this issue.
In my view the scenario you gave does not directly point to a bug, but to a feature, so I suggest closing it.
OTOH, its analysis gave rise to detecting an actual incompleteness that already exists before OpenSSL 3.0: #18708.
